Project: Next.js Notes with OpenAI Summaries

Stack
- Next.js 14 (App Router) + TypeScript
- Prisma + SQLite (dev)
- OpenAI (gpt-4o-mini) for note summaries

Model
- Note: id (string/cuid), title, content, summary, createdAt (DateTime)

API
- GET /api/notes: list notes (newest first)
- POST /api/notes: create a note; generates a 2-sentence summary via OpenAI

Quick Start
1) Install
- npm install

2) Configure env
- cp .env.example .env
- Set OPENAI_API_KEY in .env
- Optionally adjust DATABASE_URL (defaults to SQLite at file:./prisma/dev.db)

3) Initialize Prisma (dev)
- npx prisma migrate dev --name init
- This creates prisma/dev.db and the Note table.

4) Run
- npm run dev
- Open http://localhost:3000

5) Build/Start
- npm run build
- npm start

Useful
- Generate Prisma client: npm run prisma:generate
- Update schema and migrate: npm run prisma:migrate

Notes
- The API route is forced dynamic and runs on the Node.js runtime.
- Basic length guards are in place for title and content.
- Errors return JSON with an error message and appropriate status code.

Additional notes
- If you see OpenAI-related errors, ensure OPENAI_API_KEY is set and valid.
- In dev, Prisma uses a singleton client to avoid hot-reload issues.

That’s all.

